{"toolCallId":"call_274c77c8a8d84d48ab795a750892a5d3","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:19:The lifecycle is intentionally split into focused commands. `recommend-level.sh` scores a task and recommends the documentation level and optional phasing strategy. `create.sh` materializes the parent spec, optional child phases, or versioned subfolders. `upgrade-level.sh` raises an existing spec folder to a richer documentation level without discarding authored content. `calculate-completeness.sh` measures placeholder burn-down and optional content quality, `check-completion.sh` enforces checklist completion and evidence rules, and `archive.sh` archives or restores completed work with a completeness gate.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:37:Completion measurement and completion gating are separated on purpose. `calculate-completeness.sh` scans the root spec files for placeholder markers such as `[PLACEHOLDER]`, `[TODO: ...]`, and `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]`, computes per-file and overall completion percentages with `bc`, and can add quality checks for minimum word counts and required sections. `check-completion.sh` then evaluates the verification checklist in `tasks.md`, and the acceptance-criteria table when the document exists, as a release gate: it inherits priority from headings when needed, treats untagged items as blocking, requires evidence markers on completed P0 and P1 tasks, supports `--strict` to make P2 mandatory, and returns one of a fixed set of statuses such as `P0_INCOMPLETE`, `EVIDENCE_MISSING`, `AC_UNMET`, or `COMPLETE`.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:41:Archival is handled by `archive.sh`. A folder goes into the `z_archive/` beside it: `specs/z_archive/` for a packet at the specs root, the track's own `specs/<track>/z_archive/` for a packet in a track, and the parent's own `z_archive/` for a phase. A restore returns a folder to the place its archive belongs to, and the list shows every archive's entries by the path that restores them. Archives are only looked for along packet folders, the specs root, tracks and numbered packets and phases, so copies of a specs tree kept in a packet's research are never listed or restored from. After a move in a track, the script runs `refresh-track-roots.mjs` for that track, so the track root's `children_ids` stays equal to its packets and the pre-push track-root gate has nothing to block. A phase parent's `children_ids` is left as it is: its writer adds children and drops one only through a reviewed prune, so an archived phase stays listed and a restore finds it there. Before archiving, it calls `calculate-completeness.sh --json` and enforces a default 90 percent minimum unless `--force` is used or the operator confirms archiving a less-complete spec. The script also validates `NNN-name` folder naming, refuses to archive outside the specs root, detects folders already under any `z_archive/`, and uses a copy-to-temp-then-rename flow before deleting the source folder. A `z_archive/` that is a symlink is refused on archive and on restore, and `--list` leaves a linked archive out without naming it. A linked packet folder is archived by its real path when that path stays inside the specs root. An archive or restore path with a `.` or `..` segment is refused before anything resolves it, since such a segment can reach a linked `z_archive/` that the literal path does not show.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:58:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Script | Measures placeholder replacement progress and optional content quality across root spec documents |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:29:COMPLETENESS_SCRIPT=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/calculate-completeness.sh\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:66:+-- calculate-completeness.sh    # Report checklist completion metrics\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:7:# Usage: calculate-completeness.sh [OPTIONS] [SPEC_FOLDER]\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:79:  calculate-completeness.sh [OPTIONS] [SPEC_FOLDER]\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:89:  calculate-completeness.sh specs/001-feature-name/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:90:  calculate-completeness.sh --verbose specs/001-feature-name/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:91:  calculate-completeness.sh --json specs/001-feature-name/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:92:  calculate-completeness.sh --file specs/001-feature-name/spec.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh:93:  calculate-completeness.sh --quality specs/001-feature-name/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:43:3. `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/test-fixtures/063-template-compliant-level3 --json`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:142:Command 3: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/test-fixtures/063-template-compliant-level3 --json`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/speckit-completion-exposer.md:22:`system-speckit-completion` is a read-only, fail-open OpenCode `tool.register` plugin exposing one merged completion-state payload for a spec folder: inferred level (1/2/3, from canonical-doc presence), checklist P0/P1/P2 completion with evidence gaps (shelling `check-completion.sh --json`), and placeholder completeness percentage (shelling `calculate-completeness.sh --json`) -- replacing a hand-composed, hand-merged pair of Bash calls at the COMPLETION VERIFICATION gate. It ships as:\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/speckit-completion-exposer.md:37:- Real user-facing trigger: an agent operating under the COMPLETION VERIFICATION gate calls the OpenCode tool `system_speckit_completion({specFolder, strict})` (or, from Claude, runs the CLI shim) instead of hand-composing and hand-merging separate `check-completion.sh --json` and `calculate-completeness.sh --json` calls.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/speckit-completion-exposer.md:51:an agent operating under the COMPLETION VERIFICATION gate calls the OpenCode tool `system_speckit_completion({specFolder, strict})` (or, from Claude, runs the CLI shim) instead of hand-composing and hand-merging separate `check-completion.sh --json` and `calculate-completeness.sh --json` calls\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/speckit-completion-exposer.md:159:- Shelled scripts merged by the core: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:545:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:621:| `calculate-completeness.sh` | calculate spec folder completeness as a percentage |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:571:| Completeness | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"014d51","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2ace23add28344ad95a7466f7d889ab7","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:61:| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-62-| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-67-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-69-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-70-### AC_CLOSURE\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-71-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-73-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-75-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-77-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-79-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-80-**Failure modes:**\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-81-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-82-| Condition | Result |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-83-|---|---|\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-90-| An `Unmet` row while the packet is still in progress | `info` — work in progress is expected to carry open criteria |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-91-| Pre-cutoff packet | `info` — grandfathered |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-92-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-93-**Waiver contract:** a criterion may only be dropped or replaced through a decision record. The Waiver cell must name `ADR-NNN`, and every ADR it names must be declared in `decision-record.md` as a heading, a bold list item or a table row, outside any code fence. `ADR-1` and `ADR-001` are the same record.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-94-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-95-**Column binding:** the criteria table is parsed by header name, not by column position, so an escaped pipe or an added column cannot shift the Status cell.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-96-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-97-### FRONTMATTER_VALUES\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-98-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-99-`FRONTMATTER_VALUES` checks the `contextType` and `importance_tier` values in a packet's top-level docs against `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json`. It is registered at WARNING severity and never fails a run.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-100-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-101-**Rule ID:** `FRONTMATTER_VALUES`\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:585:## 9. COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-586-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-587-**Severity:** WARNING\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-588-**Description:** Validates that declared complexity level matches actual content metrics (user stories, phases, tasks).\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-589-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-590-### Expected Ranges by Level\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-591-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-592-| Level | User Stories | Phases  | Tasks     |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-593-| ----- | ------------ | ------- | --------- |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-594-| 1     | 1-2          | 2-3     | 5-15      |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-595-| 2     | 2-4          | 3-5     | 15-50     |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-596-| 3/3+  | 4-15         | 5-12    | 50-200    |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-597-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-598-### Detection Patterns\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-599-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-600-| Metric       | Pattern Searched                           |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-601-| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-602-| User Stories | `### User Story` headers in spec.md        |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-603-| Phases       | `### Phase` headers in plan.md             |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-604-| Tasks        | `- [ ] T##` or `- [ ] TASK-` in tasks.md   |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-605-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-606-### Examples\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-607-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-608-**Warning (under-scoped for Level 2):**\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-609-```\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-610-Declared Level: 2\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-611-Found: 1 user story, 2 phases, 8 tasks\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-612-Expected: 2-4 stories, 3-5 phases, 15-50 tasks\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-613-```\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-614-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-615-**Warning (over-scoped for Level 1):**\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-616-```\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-617-Declared Level: 1\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-618-Found: 5 user stories, 6 phases, 45 tasks\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-619-Expected: 1-2 stories, 2-3 phases, 5-15 tasks\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-620-```\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-621-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-622-### How to Fix\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-623-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-624-Either adjust the declared level or modify content to match:\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md-625-\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"777215","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
